      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 9.A — Parametric slope",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>For \\( x=t^3,\\ y=t^2 \\), find \\( \\dfrac{dy}{dx} \\).</p><p>Differentiate each: \\( \\dfrac{dx}{dt}=3t^2 \\), \\( \\dfrac{dy}{dt}=2t \\). Then</p>\\[ \\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{2t}{3t^2}=\\frac{2}{3t}. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 9.B — Polar area",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Find the area enclosed by the cardioid \\( r=1+\\cos\\theta \\).</p><p>Apply \\( A=\\tfrac12\\int_0^{2\\pi} r^2\\,d\\theta \\) with \\( r^2=1+2\\cos\\theta+\\cos^2\\theta \\):</p>\\[ A=\\frac12\\int_0^{2\\pi}\\big(1+2\\cos\\theta+\\cos^2\\theta\\big)\\,d\\theta=\\frac{3\\pi}{2}. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Parametric and polar calculus",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Parametric curves express \\( x \\) and \\( y \\) in terms of a parameter \\( t \\). Polar coordinates use \\( (r,\\theta) \\). Both require adapted formulas for slopes, arc lengths, and areas.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Parametric slope",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\dfrac{dy}{dx}=\\dfrac{dy/dt}{dx/dt} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Parametric arc length",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( L=\\int_a^b\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{dx}{dt}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{dy}{dt}\\right)^2}\\,dt \\)",
              "ar": null
            },
            "wide": true
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Polar area",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( A=\\dfrac{1}{2}\\int_\\alpha^\\beta r^2\\,d\\theta \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Polar to rect.",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( x=r\\cos\\theta,\\; y=r\\sin\\theta \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Find \\( \\dfrac{dy}{dx} \\) for \\( x=t^2 \\), \\( y=t^3 \\).</p>\\[ \\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{3t^2}{2t}=\\frac{3t}{2}. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example — polar area",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Area enclosed by \\( r=2\\cos\\theta \\), a circle of radius 1:</p>\\[ A=\\frac{1}{2}\\int_{-\\pi/2}^{\\pi/2}4\\cos^2\\theta\\,d\\theta = \\pi. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
